  "description": "GIVGAX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C57 H66 Br4 Dy4 N12 O23,2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.883-3.889 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.57-111.89°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(CO3)L4(acac)2(CH3OH)2(CH2OH)2]·2CH3OH (C59H72Br4Dy4N12O25; H2L = 2-(hydroxyimino)-2-[(5-bromo-2-hydroxyphenyl)methylene]hydrazide).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
